.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH speak-weather-google 1  "google " 
.SH NAME
speak\-weather\-google \- Use Google Cloud TTS engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBspeak\-weather google\fR [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-report\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-temp\-unit\fR] [\fB\-\-periods\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-audio\-format\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-voice\fR] [\fB\-\-voice\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-gain\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fILOCATION\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Use Google Cloud TTS engine
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-report\fR \fI<REPORT>\fR [default: metar]
What to announce
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
metar: Current conditions at an airport, from aviationweather.gov
.IP \(bu 2
forecast: The National Weather Service forecast (US only)
.IP \(bu 2
alerts: Active National Weather Service alerts (US only)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: speech]
Output format for the metar announcement
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
speech: Direct speech output
.IP \(bu 2
brief: Brief announcement format, without the station name
.IP \(bu 2
detailed: Detailed weather report
.IP \(bu 2
aviation: Aviation radio style
.RE
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-temp\-unit\fR \fI<TEMP_UNIT>\fR [default: fahrenheit]
Temperature unit for metar (the detailed format always gives both)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
fahrenheit
.IP \(bu 2
celsius
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-periods\fR \fI<PERIODS>\fR
Number of half\-day forecast periods [default: 2]
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Save output to file instead of speaking/printing
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-audio\-format\fR \fI<AUDIO_FORMAT>\fR
Audio format for the output file [default: from its extension, else mp3]
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
mp3: MP3 format
.IP \(bu 2
wav: WAV format (uncompressed)
.IP \(bu 2
ogg: OGG format
.IP \(bu 2
ulaw: ULAW format (8\-bit G.711)
.IP \(bu 2
alaw: ALAW format (8\-bit G.711)
.IP \(bu 2
gsm: GSM format (telephony)
.IP \(bu 2
sln16: Raw 16\-bit signed linear at 16 kHz, for Asterisk to convert as each channel needs
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-voice\fR \fI<VOICE>\fR [default: default]
Voice to use for speech
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
default: Default voice
.IP \(bu 2
us\-female: US English female voice
.IP \(bu 2
us\-male: US English male voice
.IP \(bu 2
uk\-female: UK English female voice
.IP \(bu 2
uk\-male: UK English male voice
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-voice\-name\fR \fI<VOICE_NAME>\fR
Any Google voice by its full name, such as en\-US\-Chirp3\-HD\-Leda (overrides \-\-voice)
.TP
\fB\-\-gain\fR \fI<GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
Volume relative to the voice\*(Aqs native level, in dB (\-96 to 16)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fILOCATION\fR>
ICAO airport for metar (e.g., KSJC); station, lat,lon or US address for forecast and alerts
